;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: hj2-port-obs.gc
;; name in dgo: hj2-port-obs
;; dgos: HPT

;; og:jak2-haven-city Level code for hj2-port, Jak 2's port district (ctyport): the barges sailing
;; the port's canals (levels/city/ctyport-obs.gc there). They are Jak 3's own barge and
;; boat-manager (Jak 3's ctyport-obs.o, linked just before this file in the same DGO, and Jak 3's
;; barge-ag, in this DGO too): Jak 3's code is Jak 2's, but for three things these subclasses undo.
;;   - Jak 3's barge belongs to its own level ctyport (its art is looked up there): hj2-barge belongs
;;     to hj2-port, which holds barge-ag.
;;   - Jak 3 parks the barges of the third path: Jak 2's all sail.
;;   - Jak 2's boat-manager reads its 4 paths from 4 time samples of one 'path lump, which the level
;;     port can't write (the builder writes one sample): the paths are below, as static data.
;; The barges are rigid-body vehicles steering on the port's water nav mesh (Jak 2's nav-mesh-actor
;; lump, aid 26081, exported in hj2-port-nav.json); Jak is carried when he stands on one, and
;; crushed if he stays under one for a second (Jak 3's rule). Silent: Jak 2's barge-engine and
;; bow-wash sounds are only in its PORTRUN1 bank (the port race), which the port doesn't load. Not
;; ported: Jak 2's lone barge-1 actor, idle at the bottom of
;; the water (the boat-manager spawns the fleet).

;; Paths ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

;; Jak 2's 4 barge loops (boat-manager-1's 'path lump, samples 0 to 3: closed uniform cubic
;; B-splines, their 3 first control points repeated at the end), as points on the curves: 2 per span,
;; the first repeated at the end to close the loop (generated from
;; decompiler_out/jak2/entities/ctyport-actors.json). On the curves, not on the control points:
;; these lie up to 60m off them, over the quays. y: the water (0, like Jak 2's points).
